plan.toml
PROGRESS.md
RUN_LOG.md
.claude/
tasks/
capabilities/

# IDE
.vscode/

# Rust build artifacts
/target/
# `crates/protocol-droid/tests/interop_rmcp/` is a *non-workspace*
# crate with its own resolver and its own `target/` directory.
# The root-only `/target/` rule above does not match it, and a
# `git add` of the interop source would otherwise drag the
# cargo fingerprint cache in with it. The leading-`/` and
# non-leading-`/` pair is what the project standard is for
# "ignore the workspace target and ignore every nested one too"
# — the root rule keeps the workspace's own `target/` out, this
# one catches the rest.
target/

# Node modules for the interop-ts-sdk fixtures. The fixtures
# `package.json` is the contract; `node_modules/` is the
# resolution of that contract on the developer's machine. CI
# populates it via `npm install` in the same step that runs
# the cross-test, so a committed copy would be both redundant
# and a way for a stale tree to silently replace the lockfile.
node_modules/

**/*.rs.bk

